      "text": "Let $p$ represent the cost of one pen and $x$ represent the cost of a pencil.\n\nFrom the given equation, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$\\begin{align*}\n4p + 3x &= 2.24 \\\\\n2p + 5x &= 1.54\n\\end{align*}$\n\nTo eliminate the variable $p$, we multiply the first equation by 2 and subtract the second equation:\n\n$\\begin{align*}\n8p + 6x &= 4.48 \\\\\n- 2p - 5x &= -1.54\n\\end{align*}$\n\nThis simplifies to $3p + x = 2.94$.\n\nNext, we multiply the second equation by 2 and subtract the first equation:\n\n$\\begin{align*}\n4p + 10x &= 3.08 \\\\\n- 8p - 6x &= -5.92\n\\end{align*}$\n\nThis simplifies to $4x = 1.84$, which means $x = 0.46$.\n\nThus, the cost of a pencil is \\boxed{46} cents.",
