      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Let's denote the price of a pen by \\( p \\) and the price of a pencil by \\( c \\).\n\nThe first piece of information tells us:\n\\[ 4p + 3c = 224 \\]\n\nThe second piece of information tells us:\n\\[ 2p + 5c = 154 \\]\n\nWe can solve this system of equations step by step.\n\nFirst, we multiply the second equation by 2 to align the coefficients of \\( p \\):\n\\[ 4p + 10c = 308 \\]\n\nNow we have:\n\\[ 4p + 10c = 308 \\]\n\\[ 4p + 3c = 224 \\]\n\nSubtract the second equation from the first equation to eliminate \\( 4p \\):\n\\[ (4p + 10c) - (4p + 3c) = 308 - 224 \\]\n\\[ 7c = 84 \\]\n\\[ c = \\frac{84}{7} \\]\n\\[ c = 12 \\]\n\nSo the cost of a pencil is \\( \\boxed{12} \\) cents per pencil.\n\nCheck:\nSubstitute \\( c = 12 \\) back into the second original equation:\n\\[ 2p + 5(12) = 154 \\]\n\\[ 2p = 154 - 60 \\]\n\\[ 2p = 94 \\]\n\\[ p = 47 \\]\n\nCheck the first original equation:\n\\[ 4(47) + 3(12) = 188 + 36 = 224 \\]\n\nEverything checks out. The cost of a pencil is indeed \\(\\boxed{12}\\) cents.",
