      "text": "Let's denote the cost of a pen by \\( p \\) and the cost of a pencil by \\( c \\). We are given two equations based on the problem statement:\n\n1. Four pens and three pencils cost $2.24.\n2. Two pens and five pencils cost $1.54.\n\nWe can express these statements in mathematical form as follows:\n\n1. \\( 4p + 3c = 224 \\)\n2. \\( 2p + 5c = 154 \\)\n\nWe need to find the values of \\( p \\) and \\( c \\). Let's use the first equation as it is more straightforward to solve directly.\n\nFirst, we'll multiply the second equation by 2 to align the coefficients of \\( p \\):\n\n\\[ 2(2p + 5c) = 2 \\cdot 154 \\]\n\\[ 4p + 10c = 308 \\]\n\nNow we have the following system of equations:\n\n1. \\( 4p + 3c = 224 \\)\n2. \\( 4p + 10c = 308 \\)\n\nNext, we'll subtract the first equation from the second equation to eliminate \\( p \\):\n\n\\[ (4p + 10c) - (4p + 3c) = 308 - 224 \\]\n\\[ 4p + 10c - 4p - 3c = 84 \\]\n\\[ 7c = 84 \\]\n\nSolving for \\( c \\):\n\n\\[ c = \\frac{84}{7} \\]\n\\[ c = 12 \\]\n\nThus, the cost of a pencil is \\(\\boxed{12}\\) cents.",
